lxqt-schedule for Debian and Bianbu
=================================

The package installs lxqt-schedule, lxqt-schedule-ctl, and an XDG autostart
entry for LXQt desktop sessions. Log out and back in after installation,
or start lxqt-schedule manually from a terminal in the desktop session.

The daemon and CLI must run as the same desktop user on the same session
D-Bus. Running the daemon as root or as a system service is not required.
A desktop notification service, such as lxqt-notificationd, is needed to
display reminders.

Schedules are stored in ~/.config/lxqt/schedule.json (or under the
corresponding XDG_CONFIG_HOME). Removing the package does not remove this
per-user data. Stop the daemon before manually changing or restoring it.

Use lxqt-schedule-ctl ping to check connectivity and lxqt-schedule-ctl list
--json to inspect schedules. See README.md for command examples.

Integration resources are installed under /usr/share/doc/lxqt-schedule/.
The worldclock patch and bibit-intent skill require separate integration;
they are not automatically applied to other installed packages.
